# WISIPAY PROVIDER RESPONSE LOG (SAMPLE / DUMMY DATA — FOR ASSESSMENT USE ONLY)
# This file contains the raw response received from the payment provider for each
# transaction attempt. Every row in transactions.log that triggers a provider call
# should have a corresponding entry here.
#
# Format per line:
#   TIMESTAMP | TXN_ID=... | PROVIDER=... | PROVIDER_REF=... | RESP_CODE=... | RESP_MSG=... | LATENCY_MS=...
#
# Fields:
#   PROVIDER      — Payment gateway / bank that processed the request
#   PROVIDER_REF  — Provider's own transaction reference number
#   RESP_CODE     — Raw HTTP-style or provider-specific numeric response code
#   RESP_MSG      — Raw message string returned by the provider
#   LATENCY_MS    — Round-trip time in milliseconds between WisiPay and the provider
#
# PROVIDER CODES USED:
#   RAZORPAY   = Razorpay Payment Gateway
#   PAYU       = PayU Money Gateway
#   HDFC_PG    = HDFC Bank Payment Gateway
#   NPCI_UPI   = NPCI UPI Rails (direct)
#   AXIS_PG    = Axis Bank Payment Gateway
#   ICICI_PG   = ICICI Bank Payment Gateway
#   KOTAK_PG   = Kotak Mahindra Bank Payment Gateway
#
# NOTE: RESP_CODE 200 = success, 202 = accepted/pending, 400 = bad request,
#       401 = auth failure, 402 = limit exceeded, 403 = blocked/fraud,
#       408 = timeout, 500 = provider internal error, 502 = bad gateway,
#       503 = service unavailable

